<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pope Innocent II</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1143</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Gregorio Papareschi</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pope Innocent II, born Gregorio Papareschi, was pope from 1130 to 1143. His election was contested by the antipope Anacletus II, and with the support of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bernard-of-clairvaux">Bernard of Clairvaux</a> and the emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lothair-i">Lothair</a> III he prevailed after a long schism. He held the Second Lateran Council in 1139, and in his last years the Roman commune rose against papal rule.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pope-innocent-ii.jpg" alt="Pope Innocent II" width="320" height="504" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hugo DK · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pope_Innocent_II_%E2%80%93_Santa_Maria_in_Trastevere.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
